43. Frontend Implementation Rules for Nemotron
Use the already supplied admin dashboard repository as the base. Do not replace its layout system.
Reuse existing Shadcn components and project utilities before creating new primitives.
Build the app as reusable modules, not isolated static pages.
Create shared components for record headers, data tables, filter bars, status badges, object links, activity timelines, assignee selectors and review panels.
Use realistic CA Nexus mock data so relationships between modules can be demonstrated.
All navigation and drill-down links should function in the frontend even before backend integration.
Create route structure matching the navigation hierarchy.
Create typed frontend models/interfaces for all major objects.
Separate mock data/services from visual components so API integration can replace data sources later.
Implement loading, empty and error states for every major data screen.
Implement dialogs/sheets for create/edit flows and destructive confirmations.
Do not build pages as generic dashboards with repeated placeholder charts; operational tables, queues and actionable context are more important.
Keep client, matter and compliance context visible throughout deep workflows.
Do not expose future integrations as falsely functional; clearly represent integration-dependent actions/states in the frontend.
